      "id": "style_blend",
      "section": "Art style",
      "question": "Blend test: which mix of A and C is best?",
      "who_decides": "Both",
      "answered": true,
      "answer_values": "blend3_gloss",
      "answer_labels": "Blend 3 · Chunky with rich gloss",
      "claude_suggested": [
        "blend2_even"
      ],
      "other": "Daddy liked blend 1 because he thinks the outline makes for readable and more consistent AI artwork - Ame prefers blend 3 \"because its the shiniest - I just love it because its shiny\".",
      "answered_by": "Amelia",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-01T19:41:33.314Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "art_style",
      "section": "Art style",
      "question": "Which finish should the whole game use?",
      "who_decides": "Both",
      "answered": true,
      "answer_values": "A_gloss",
      "answer_labels": "A · Juicy gloss",
      "claude_suggested": [
        "B_handmade_gloss"
      ],
      "other": "this box has a max character limit which is annoying...",
      "note": "Answer from human parent & Amelia: we really like both A and C - the juicy gloss look and the bold and chunky look - we think that the bold chunky look will be easier to nail consistently - especially getting details right in terms of VN cut scenes or CGs etc. So I think what we really want is some blending/combination/middle point between A and C here - so the bold chunky design BUT with some more smooth polished and shiny texture / gloss.",
      "answered_by": "Amelia",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-31T20:02:01.486Z"
    },
